{"id":"mahabharata-1-143","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":143,"title":"त्रिचत्वारिंशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 143 · Bhima and Hidimba; the birth of Ghatotkacha","summary":{"en":"Bhima warns Hidimba away, but she pleads with Kunti, and Yudhishthira allows her to be with Bhima by day until she bears a son. Ghatotkacha is born, grows at once to youth, promises to come whenever needed, and departs; he was created by Indra to draw Karna's spear.","kn":"ಭೀಮನು ಹಿಡಿಂಬೆಯನ್ನು ದೂರ ಹೋಗೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಆದರೆ ಅವಳು ಕುಂತಿಯನ್ನು ಬೇಡುತ್ತಾಳೆ; ಮಗನಾಗುವವರೆಗೆ ಹಗಲು ಭೀಮನೊಂದಿಗಿರಲು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಅನುಮತಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಘಟೋತ್ಕಚನು ಜನಿಸಿ ಕೂಡಲೇ ಯುವಕನಾಗಿ, ಬೇಕಾದಾಗ ಬರುವೆನೆಂದು ಹೇಳಿ ಹೊರಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕರ್ಣನ ಶಕ್ತಿಯನ್ನು ಸೆಳೆಯಲು ಇಂದ್ರನು ಅವನನ್ನು ಸೃಷ್ಟಿಸಿದ್ದನು.","hi":"भीम हिडिम्बा को दूर जाने को कहते हैं, पर वह कुन्ती से विनती करती है, और युधिष्ठिर उसे पुत्र होने तक दिन में भीम के साथ रहने की अनुमति देते हैं। घटोत्कच जन्मता है, तुरन्त युवा होता है, आवश्यकता पर आने का वचन देकर चला जाता है; इन्द्र ने उसे कर्ण की शक्ति को खींचने के लिए रचा था।","te":"భీముడు హిడింబిని దూరంగా పొమ్మంటాడు, కానీ ఆమె కుంతిని వేడుకుంటుంది; కుమారుడు పుట్టే వరకు పగలు భీమునితో ఉండడానికి యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అనుమతిస్తాడు. ఘటోత్కచుడు పుట్టి వెంటనే యువకుడై, అవసరమైనప్పుడు వస్తానని చెప్పి వెళ్తాడు; కర్ణుని శక్తిని ఆకర్షించడానికి ఇంద్రుడు అతనిని సృష్టించాడు.","ta":"பீமன் ஹிடிம்பையை விலகிப் போகச் சொல்ல, அவள் குந்தியிடம் மன்றாடுகிறாள்; மகன் பிறக்கும் வரை பகலில் பீமனுடன் இருக்க யுதிஷ்டிரர் அனுமதிக்கிறார். கடோத்கசன் பிறந்து உடனே இளைஞனாகி, தேவைப்படும்போது வருவதாகச் சொல்லிச் செல்கிறான்; கர்ணனின் ஶக்தியை ஈர்க்க இந்திரன் அவனைப் படைத்திருந்தான்.","ml":"ഭീമൻ ഹിഡിംബയെ അകറ്റാൻ ശ്രമിക്കുന്നു, എന്നാൽ അവൾ കുന്തിയോട് അപേക്ഷിക്കുന്നു; ഒരു പുത്രനെ പ്രസവിക്കുന്നതുവരെ പകൽസമയം ഭീമനോടൊപ്പം കഴിയാൻ യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ അനുവദിക്കുന്നു. ഘടോത്കചൻ ജനിക്കുന്നു; ഉടനെ യൗവനത്തിലേക്ക് വളരുന്ന അവൻ ആവശ്യമുള്ളപ്പോഴെല്ലാം വരാമെന്ന് വാക്കുനൽകി പോകുന്നു; കർണ്ണന്റെ കുന്തം ആകർഷിക്കാൻ ഇന്ദ്രൻ സൃഷ്ടിച്ചതാണ് അവനെ."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.143; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"बकवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bakavadha Parva (Slaying of Baka)","verses":[{"text":"भीम उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhima said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"स्मरन्ति वैरं रक्षांसि मायामाश्रित्य मोहिनीम् ।\nहिडिम्बे व्रज पन्थानं त्वं वै भ्रातृनिषेवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Rakshasas remember their enmity and resort to bewildering magic. Hidimba, go the way your brother has gone.'"}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"क्रुद्धोऽपि पुरुषव्याघ्र भीम मा स्म स्त्रियं वधीः ।\nशरीरगुप्त्याभ्यधिकं धर्मं गोपय पाण्डव ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Even in anger, Bhima, tiger among men, do not kill a woman. Guard dharma above even guarding your body, Pandava."}},{"n":3,"text":"वधाभिप्रायमायान्तमवधीस्त्वं महाबलम् ।\nरक्षसस्तस्य भगिनी किं नः क्रुद्धा करिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"'You killed the mighty one who came intending to kill us. What can his sister do to us, even angry?'"}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"हिडिम्बा तु ततः कुन्तीमभिवाद्य कृताञ्जलिः ।\nयुधिष्ठिरं च कौन्तेयमिदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Hidimba bowed to Kunti and to Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, with joined palms, and spoke these words."}},{"n":5,"text":"आर्ये जानासि यद्दुःखमिह स्त्रीणामनङ्गजम् ।\nतदिदं मामनुप्राप्तं भीमसेनकृतं शुभे ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Noble lady, you know the sorrow born of love that women feel here. That very sorrow, good lady, has come upon me through Bhimasena."}},{"n":6,"text":"सोढं तत्परमं दुःखं मया कालप्रतीक्षया ।\nसोऽयमभ्यागतः कालो भविता मे सुखाय वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"'I have borne that great sorrow waiting for the right time. That time has come, and it will surely bring me happiness."}},{"n":7,"text":"मया ह्युत्सृज्य सुहृदः स्वधर्मं स्वजनं तथा ।\nवृतोऽयं पुरुषव्याघ्रस्तव पुत्रः पतिः शुभे ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Having abandoned my friends, my own duty and my kin, I have chosen your son, this tiger among men, as my husband, good lady."}},{"n":8,"text":"वरेणापि तथानेन त्वया चापि यशस्विनि ।\nतथा ब्रुवन्ती हि तदा प्रत्याख्याता क्रियां प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Though I spoke so, both he and you turned me down when it came to the act."}},{"n":9,"text":"त्वं मां मूढेति वा मत्वा भक्ता वानुगतेति वा ।\nभर्त्रानेन महाभागे संयोजय सुतेन ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Whether you think me foolish or a loyal follower, great lady, unite me with this son of yours as my husband."}},{"n":10,"text":"तमुपादाय गच्छेयं यथेष्टं देवरूपिणम् ।\nपुनश्चैवागमिष्यामि विश्रम्भं कुरु मे शुभे ॥","meaning":{"en":"'I will take him, godlike, and go where I please, and I will come back again. Trust me, good lady."}},{"n":11,"text":"अहं हि मनसा ध्याता सर्वान्नेष्यामि वः सदा ।\nवृजिने तारयिष्यामि दुर्गेषु च नरर्षभान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Whenever you think of me, I will carry you all. I will bring you across trouble and through difficult places, bulls among men."}},{"n":12,"text":"पृष्ठेन वो वहिष्यामि शीघ्रां गतिमभीप्सतः ।\nयूयं प्रसादं कुरुत भीमसेनो भजेत माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"'I will carry you on my back if you want to go fast. Please be kind, and let Bhimasena be mine."}},{"n":13,"text":"आपदस्तरणे प्राणान्धारयेद्येन येन हि ।\nसर्वमादृत्य कर्तव्यं तद्धर्ममनुवर्तता ॥","meaning":{"en":"'To cross a calamity, whatever keeps one's life going should be done with care, following dharma."}},{"n":14,"text":"आपत्सु यो धारयति धर्मं धर्मविदुत्तमः ।\nव्यसनं ह्येव धर्मस्य धर्मिणामापदुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Whoever holds to dharma in disasters is the best knower of dharma; for disaster is the real trial of dharma among the righteous."}},{"n":15,"text":"पुण्यं प्राणान्धारयति पुण्यं प्राणदमुच्यते ।\nयेन येनाचरेद्धर्मं तस्मिन्गर्हा न विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"'What preserves life is merit, and merit is said to give life. By whatever means one practices dharma, no blame attaches.'"}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"एवमेतद्यथात्थ त्वं हिडिम्बे नात्र संशयः ।\nस्थातव्यं तु त्वया धर्मे यथा ब्रूयां सुमध्यमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"'It is just as you say, Hidimba, without doubt. But you must stay with dharma as I tell you, slender-waisted one."}},{"n":17,"text":"स्नातं कृताह्निकं भद्रे कृतकौतुकमङ्गलम् ।\nभीमसेनं भजेथास्त्वं प्रागस्तगमनाद्रवेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Bathe, finish your daily rites, put on the auspicious marks, and go to Bhimasena before the sun sets."}},{"n":18,"text":"अहःसु विहरानेन यथाकामं मनोजवा ।\nअयं त्वानयितव्यस्ते भीमसेनः सदा निशि ॥","meaning":{"en":"'By day roam with him as you wish, swift as thought; but you must bring Bhimasena back to us every night.'"}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"तथेति तत्प्रतिज्ञाय हिडिम्बा राक्षसी तदा ।\nभीमसेनमुपादाय ऊर्ध्वमाचक्रमे ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The rakshasi Hidimba agreed, 'So be it,' took Bhimasena and rose into the air."}},{"n":20,"text":"शैलशृङ्गेषु रम्येषु देवतायतनेषु च ।\nमृगपक्षिविघुष्टेषु रमणीयेषु सर्वदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"On delightful mountain peaks and in temples of the gods, always pleasant places loud with beasts and birds,"}},{"n":21,"text":"कृत्वा च परमं रूपं सर्वाभरणभूषिता ।\nसंजल्पन्ती सुमधुरं रमयामास पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"taking a most beautiful form and adorned with every ornament, she delighted the Pandava with sweet conversation."}},{"n":22,"text":"तथैव वनदुर्गेषु पुष्पितद्रुमसानुषु ।\nसरःसु रमणीयेषु पद्मोत्पलयुतेषु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"So too in forest fastnesses, on slopes of flowering trees, by lovely lakes with lotuses and water lilies,"}},{"n":23,"text":"नदीद्वीपप्रदेशेषु वैडूर्यसिकतासु च ।\nसुतीर्थवनतोयासु तथा गिरिनदीषु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"on river islands with sands of cat's-eye gems, along fine bathing places, forest waters and mountain streams,"}},{"n":24,"text":"सगरस्य प्रदेशेषु मणिहेमचितेषु च ।\nपत्तनेषु च रम्येषु महाशालवनेषु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"in coastal regions of the ocean strewn with jewels and gold, in lovely towns and great sal forests,"}},{"n":25,"text":"देवारण्येषु पुण्येषु तथा पर्वतसानुषु ।\nगुह्यकानां निवासेषु तापसायतनेषु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"in holy divine forests, on mountain slopes, in the abodes of Guhyakas and hermitages of ascetics,"}},{"n":26,"text":"सर्वर्तुफलपुष्पेषु मानसेषु सरःसु च ।\nबिभ्रती परमं रूपं रमयामास पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and by the Manasa lakes with fruits and flowers in every season, she kept her fairest form and delighted the Pandava."}},{"n":27,"text":"रमयन्ती तथा भीमं तत्र तत्र मनोजवा ।\nप्रजज्ञे राक्षसी पुत्रं भीमसेनान्महाबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As she thus delighted Bhima here and there, swift as thought, the rakshasi bore a very strong son to Bhimasena."}},{"n":28,"text":"विरूपाक्षं महावक्त्रं शङ्कुकर्णं विभीषणम् ।\nभीमरूपं सुताम्रोष्ठं तीक्ष्णदंष्ट्रं महाबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He had fearsome eyes, a huge mouth, ears like stakes, a terrifying look, deep-red lips, sharp fangs and great strength."}},{"n":29,"text":"महेष्वासं महावीर्यं महासत्त्वं महाभुजम् ।\nमहाजवं महाकायं महामायमरिंदमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great archer of great prowess, great spirit and mighty arms, very swift, huge of body, a master of great illusions, a tamer of foes."}},{"n":30,"text":"अमानुषं मानुषजं भीमवेगं महाबलम् ।\nयः पिशाचानतीवान्यान्बभूवाति स मानुषान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not human though born of a man, of terrible speed and great strength, he surpassed other pishachas and also men."}},{"n":31,"text":"बालोऽपि यौवनं प्राप्तो मानुषेषु विशां पते ।\nसर्वास्त्रेषु परं वीरः प्रकर्षमगमद्बली ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though newborn, he reached youth among humans, lord of the people, and the strong hero attained supreme mastery of all weapons."}},{"n":32,"text":"सद्यो हि गर्भं राक्षस्यो लभन्ते प्रसवन्ति च ।\nकामरूपधराश्चैव भवन्ति बहुरूपिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For rakshasis conceive and give birth at once, and they take shapes at will and many forms."}},{"n":33,"text":"प्रणम्य विकचः पादावगृह्णात्स पितुस्तदा ।\nमातुश्च परमेष्वासस्तौ च नामास्य चक्रतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bowing, the hairless child took his father's and mother's feet, and the two gave him his name."}},{"n":34,"text":"घटभासोत्कच इति मातरं सोऽभ्यभाषत ।\nअभवत्तेन नामास्य घटोत्कच इति स्म ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Since he spoke to his mother as a bald 'pot-head' (ghata-utkacha), his name was Ghatotkacha."}},{"n":35,"text":"अनुरक्तश्च तानासीत्पाण्डवान्स घटोत्कचः ।\nतेषां च दयितो नित्यमात्मभूतो बभूव सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ghatotkacha was devoted to the Pandavas, and he became ever dear to them, as if one of themselves."}},{"n":36,"text":"संवाससमयो जीर्ण इत्यभाषत तं ततः ।\nहिडिम्बा समयं कृत्वा स्वां गतिं प्रत्यपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, saying that the agreed time of living together was over, Hidimba made a pact and went her own way."}},{"n":37,"text":"कृत्यकाल उपस्थास्ये पितॄनिति घटोत्कचः ।\nआमन्त्र्य राक्षसश्रेष्ठः प्रतस्थे चोत्तरां दिशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ghatotkacha said, 'I will attend my fathers when the time calls,' took leave, and the best of rakshasas set off northward."}},{"n":38,"text":"स हि सृष्टो मघवता शक्तिहेतोर्महात्मना ।\nकर्णस्याप्रतिवीर्यस्य विनाशाय महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was created by great Indra, for the sake of a spear, to bring about the destruction of the great and unmatched Karna."}}]}]}